1. **A computer-implemented method for delivering delayed video and synchronized subtitles to a viewer terminal over a communication network, the method comprising:**

receiving, by a media delivery system, a video stream comprising video content and timing information;

storing at least a portion of the video stream in a video buffer to impose a delivery delay relative to receipt of the video stream;

obtaining subtitle data corresponding to the video content, the subtitle data comprising subtitle text associated with respective presentation timestamps;

determining a playback timeline for the buffered video stream based at least in part on the timing information and the delivery delay;

synchronizing the subtitle data with the buffered video stream by mapping the respective presentation timestamps to the playback timeline;

transmitting, over the communication network to the viewer terminal, the buffered video stream in accordance with the playback timeline; and

transmitting, over the communication network to the viewer terminal, the synchronized subtitle data such that each subtitle text is presented by the viewer terminal in temporal alignment with a corresponding portion of the delayed video content.

1. **A communication apparatus comprising:**

a communication unit configured to communicate with a video source, a subtitler terminal, and a viewer terminal; and

a controller configured to:

receive, via the communication unit, original video from the video source;

generate delayed video by delaying presentation of the original video by a delay interval;

provide information representing at least a portion of the original video to the subtitler terminal;

obtain, from the subtitler terminal via the communication unit, subtitles corresponding to the at least a portion of the original video;

synchronize the subtitles with the delayed video based on the delay interval; and

cause the communication unit to transmit the delayed video and the synchronized subtitles to the viewer terminal for presentation of the subtitles in temporal correspondence with the delayed video.

**1. A computer-implemented method for synchronizing subtitle data with a video stream, the method comprising:**

receiving, by a media processing system, an input video stream;

applying, by the media processing system, a first temporal delay to the input video stream to generate a delayed video stream;

transmitting at least a portion of the input video stream, prior to application of the first temporal delay, to a captioning terminal;

receiving, from the captioning terminal, subtitle data corresponding to the at least a portion of the input video stream and delay information indicative of a captioning delay;

determining, based at least in part on the first temporal delay and the delay information, a display time for the subtitle data relative to the delayed video stream; and

transmitting, to an audience terminal, the delayed video stream and the subtitle data such that the subtitle data is presented at the determined display time in synchronization with corresponding content of the delayed video stream.
